<writing_rules>
SENTENCE RULES:
- 1500–2000 words total. First 20 words must contain the core premise.
- Complete sentences only. Active voice. 12–18 words per sentence average.
- Vary rhythm: a 6-word sentence next to a 24-word sentence creates engagement.
- Paragraphs: 3–5 sentences max. Natural flow — no bullet points or fragments.

STRUCTURE:
- Hook at the start to grab attention in the first 10 seconds.
- Clear intro → body → conclusion arc.
- Conversational tone — write as if explaining to a knowledgeable friend.
- End with a call to action (like/subscribe) woven naturally into the conclusion.

BANNED PHRASES — never use these:
- Dialogue in quotation marks. Use: He admitted the plan was flawed.
- Parentheses, brackets, or dashes as stage directions.
- Markdown formatting, bold, italics, code blocks.
- Creator intros: Hey guys, Welcome back, Today we are looking at.
- Filler transitions: In conclusion, To summarize, As we can see.
- Passive voice: The player discovers — NOT: It is discovered by the player.
- "You" in the script body. Keep focus on game/characters.

CHARACTER RULES — use positive framing:
- USE ONLY characters listed in VERIFIED CONTEXT above.
- Reference characters by their canonical names (use the name mappings provided).
- If you must reference an unnamed person, use: "a character", "the survivor", "one player".
- Describe only events explicitly in the transcript — do not infer motivations or backstories.
</writing_rules>

<title_rules>
TITLE: 6–10 words. Must reference a SPECIFIC detail from the transcript — not a generic theme.
Structures (rotate across scripts):
  question: What Made X Impossible?
  statement: The One Rule That Broke Y
  contrast: X Was Simple. Then Z Happened.
  number: 3 Seconds That Ruined Everything
  reveal: Why X Never Told Y the Truth
Avoid: The [Noun] of [Noun], all-caps, clickbait that overpromises.
</title_rules>

<description_rules>
DESCRIPTION: 2–3 sentences. Complements the title — does NOT repeat it.
Open with a verb that is NOT in the banned list or recent openers.
End with 3–5 lowercase hashtags. Game name first.
</description_rules>

<tag_rules>
TAGS: 10–15 comma-separated keywords, strictly lowercase.
Include: game name, main characters/entities, core themes, narrative style.
</tag_rules>

<output_format>
Output exactly this format — nothing else:

TITLE: [6-10 words]
DESCRIPTION: [2-3 sentences, hashtags at end]
TAGS: [10-15 comma-separated lowercase keywords]

[Script body — 1500-2000 words. Separated from TAGS by exactly one blank line.]

Rules:
- No markdown code blocks around the output.
- No text before TITLE: or after the script body.
- The blank line between TAGS and body = exactly one newline.
</output_format>
